@notice Sentinel address used by IndexToken baskets to refer to
         this adapter's native asset (e.g. a stable, non-colliding
         address derived from the asset name).

@notice Default deposit expiry offset above `block.timestamp`,
         in seconds. THORChain requires ≥ 3600. Defaulted to 7200
         to give the Router transaction comfortable headroom.

@notice Maximum age (seconds) of the registry's vault cache that
         `acquire` will accept. THORChain Asgard rotates per churn
         (~3 days) with retired vaults active for ~6 hours;
         12 hours is a comfortable bot-SLA + grace margin.

@dev THORChain memo asset string, e.g. "BTC.BTC". Set in constructor;
      not modifiable. Stored in storage because Solidity has no
      `immutable string`.

@dev String form of our native-chain custody address, e.g. a
      Bitcoin bech32 multisig. Owner-rotatable; new mints route to
      whatever this is set to at call time.

@param dispatchId Per-adapter unique id (binds a nonce) for
        executor deduplication.
 @param redemptionId The IntentQueue redemption this leg settles.
 @param targetToken The async native-asset sentinel redeemed.
 @param amount Native amount to send from custody to THORChain.
 @param destination The IndexToken that receives the swapped USDT.
 @param memo Canonical `=:ETH.USDT:<destination>:<minOutUsdt>` memo
        the executor uses for the native-chain-side Asgard deposit.

@param initialOwner Owner permitted to rotate the native custody address.
 @param factory_ {IIndexFactory} whose registered IndexToken clones are
        the only authorized callers of the dispatch entry-points.
 @param router_ THORChain Ethereum Router. Mainnet: `0xD37BbE5744D730a1d98d8DC97c42F0Ca46aD7146`.
 @param vaultRegistry_ The {ThorchainVaultRegistry} that mirrors the current Asgard vault.
 @param targetTokenSentinel Stable address used in IndexToken
        baskets to refer to this asset (factory allowlists this).
 @param memoAsset_ THORChain asset string for the swap memo (e.g. "BTC.BTC").
 @param nativeCustodyAddress_ Initial native-chain destination (our multisig address).

@notice Rotates the native-chain destination address. Owner-only.
 @dev   Affects all future deposits. In-flight intents already
        directed at the previous address must settle to the
        previous address — by design, off-chain ops should pause
        new mints during rotation, drain or reconcile in-flight
        intents, then update.

@notice Recover ERC20 tokens accidentally left in this adapter.
 @dev   Last-resort path for funds stuck if e.g. the Router fails to
        pull an approved deposit (broken-router scenario). Owner-only;
        `forceApprove(0)` at the end of `acquire` already prevents
        post-tx pulls, so this only applies to genuinely orphaned
        tokens. Reverts if the contract has zero balance to make
        accidental misuse loud.

@inheritdoc IAssetAdapter
 @dev   Returns 0 because settlement is asynchronous. The
        IndexToken records expected/attested amounts via
        `IAsyncAssetAdapter.previewAsync` and the IntentQueue.
 @param hints ABI-encoded `(uint256 minOutNativeUnits)` — passed
        through to THORChain's `LIM` field on the swap memo.

@dev Builds a THORChain swap memo of the form
      `=:ASSET:DESTADDR:MIN`. Memo size cap is 250 bytes; for our
      typical (asset, address, minOut) sizes we are well under.
